Third-party components

The renderer uses two libraries, run only when a booklet has a diagram or a
formula to draw: Temml is stored inside booklet.html, and mermaid is the file
parts/mermaid.js beside it (the one-file build, made by test/one-file.js, stores
both inside one file). Both are MIT licensed, and their copyright notices are kept
in the comments above their places in booklet.html.

- mermaid (@mermaid-js/tiny 12.1.0), https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid
  The MIT License (MIT). Copyright (c) 2014 - 2022 Knut Sveidqvist.
  The bundle also carries other open-source packages under their own
  licences, named in the package.
- Temml 0.13.5, https://github.com/ronkok/Temml
  The MIT License (MIT). Copyright (c) 2020 Ron Kok.

booklet.html also carries pictures and fonts, as data inside the file (renderer
0.11.8). Nothing is fetched; their notices are kept in the comments beside them
in booklet.html and in art/.

